 "best_diff": "--- initial\n+++ best\n@@ -18,8 +18,22 @@\n     Every row must give the same number of features. The classifier is linear in the\n     features (they are standardized and a bias is added), so nonlinear structure only\n     helps if a feature expresses it. Only the Python standard library may be used.\n-\n-    Current method: the raw inputs.\n     \"\"\"\n-    return list(row)\n+    x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6 = row\n+    feats = []\n+    # Raw inputs\n+    feats.extend([x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6])\n+    # Squares\n+    feats.extend([x1*x1, x2*x2, x3*x3, x4*x4, x5*x5, x6*x6])\n+    # Log of x3 to handle right-skewed distribution\n+    feats.append(math.log(x3) if x3 > 0 else -10.0)\n+    # Pairwise products (selected pairs likely to matter)\n+    feats.extend([x1*x2, x1*x3, x1*x4, x1*x5, x1*x6])\n+    feats.extend([x2*x3, x2*x4, x2*x5, x2*x6])\n+    feats.extend([x3*x4, x3*x5, x3*x6])\n+    feats.extend([x4*x5, x4*x6])\n+    feats.append(x5*x6)\n+    # Sign products for quadrant-sensitive patterns\n+    feats.extend([math.copysign(1, x1*x2), math.copysign(1, x1*x3)])\n+    return feats\n # OMEGA-BLOCK-END\n",
